[components.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/components.mdc)

You are an expert in Astro, React, TypeScript, and TailwindCSS for scalable web development.

Key Principles
- Write concise, technical responses with accurate Astro and React examples
- Leverage Astro's partial hydration with React components effectively
- This is an SSR application using Node adapter (not static generation)
- Use TypeScript for type safety across all components
- Follow shadcn/ui component patterns and best practices

Project Structure
- astro-app/
    - src/
        - components/
            - ui/          # shadcn/ui components
            - [various]/  # feature-specific React components
        - layouts/        # Astro layouts (BaseLayout.astro, Layout.astro)
        - pages/         # Astro pages and API routes
        - lib/          # utility functions, data fetching, type definitions
        - stores/       # nanostores (query.ts, settings.ts)
        - actions/      # Astro actions (server-side functions)
    - public/          # static assets
    - astro.config.mjs # Astro configuration (Node adapter, SSR)
    - tsconfig.json

Component Development
- Create .astro files for page layouts and static components
- Use .tsx files for React components that need interactivity
- Implement strict TypeScript typing for all components
- Follow common React component patterns (see [react-components.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/react-components.mdc))
- Keep React components simple and focused on UI concerns
- Use shadcn/ui components as the foundation for UI elements
- Import types from `@/lib/definitions` for shared data types (see [data-types.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/data-types.mdc))
- Use Astro's component props with TypeScript interfaces

Styling Guidelines
- Use TailwindCSS v4 (via @tailwindcss/vite plugin) exclusively for styling
- Follow utility-first CSS approach (see [react-components.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/react-components.mdc) for common styling rules)
- Never use custom CSS or @apply directives
- Maintain consistent spacing using Tailwind's spacing scale
- Use Tailwind's color palette for consistency
- Implement responsive design using Tailwind breakpoints (sm:, md:, lg:, xl:)
- Configuration is done via Tailwind CSS v4 (no separate config file needed)

Astro Actions
- Actions are defined in `astro-app/src/actions/index.ts` and exported as `server` object
- Use `defineAction` from `astro:actions` to create actions
- Actions accept `accept: 'json'` or `accept: 'form'` depending on use case
- Use `ActionError` from `astro:actions` for client-visible errors
- Actions can access `locals` (user, PocketBase instance), `cookies`, `request`, etc.
- Call actions from Astro pages using `Astro.callAction(actions.*.*, input)` (e.g., `Astro.callAction(actions.users.getUserProfile, { username })`)
- Call actions from React components using `actions.*.*()` from `astro:actions` (e.g., `actions.picks.submitPick()`, `actions.users.login()`)

Data Fetching
- Server-side: Use `Astro.callAction()` or direct function calls in `.astro` files
- Client-side: Use React Query with actions (see react-fetching-data.mdc)
- React Query client is managed via nanostores in `astro-app/src/stores/query.ts`
- Always use `useStore(queryClient)` to get the QueryClient instance in React components
- Pass the QueryClient instance as the second parameter to `useQuery` and `useMutation` hooks

React Component Guidelines
- Keep components as simple as possible
- Use TypeScript interfaces for props
- Use React Query hooks (`useQuery`, `useMutation`) with actions for data fetching
- Follow shadcn/ui patterns for consistency
- Use `client:*` directives appropriately (load, idle, visible)

TypeScript Best Practices
- Enable strict mode in tsconfig.json
- Define interfaces for all props and data structures
- Use Zod schemas in `astro-app/src/lib/definitions.ts` for runtime validation
- Import types using `type` keyword when importing only types
- Use `@/` alias for imports (configured in tsconfig.json)

Server-Side Rendering
- This project uses SSR with Node adapter in standalone mode
- Access user state via `Astro.locals.isAuthed` and `Astro.locals.user`
- Use PocketBase instance from `Astro.locals.pb` for database operations
- Environment variables are accessed via `astro:env/server` and `astro:env/client`

Accessibility
- Follow WCAG guidelines
- Implement proper ARIA attributes
- Ensure keyboard navigation
- Use semantic HTML elements

Code Quality
- Keep components modular and reusable
- Document complex logic with clear comments
- Use consistent naming conventions
- Follow existing code patterns in the codebase

Refer to Astro's official documentation (v5.6+) and shadcn/ui documentation for detailed component implementation guidelines.
